@@ -69,6 +69,25 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
+Printing JSON
+-------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.print_json` method pretty prints a JSON string with syntax highlighting. The output is valid JSON, indented with 4 spaces by default; pass ``indent`` to change the number of spaces, and ``highlight=False`` to disable highlighting::
+
+    >>> console.print_json('[false, true, null, "foo"]', indent=2)
+
+You can also log a :class:`~rich.json.JSON` renderable with :meth:`~rich.console.Console.print` or :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log`. Long lines are not wrapped.
+
+The ``print_json`` function is also available at package level, using the global console::
+
+    from rich import print_json
+
+    print_json('[false, true, null, "foo"]')
+
+JSON can also be pretty printed from the command line by running the json module with a path to a file::
+
+    python -m rich.json FILE
+
